    "content_mXUFDG": {
      "type": "content",
      "settings": {
        "padding_top": 0,
        "padding_bottom": 4.8,
        "padding_top_desktop": 0,
        "padding_bottom_desktop": 12.6,
        "content": "<h2>Find Your Perfect Lip</h2><p>You’ve made Lip Butter Balm an Allure Best of Beauty Award-winner and Sephora best-seller so you’re probably wondering if you need both Dream Lip Oil and Lip Butter Balm. The answer is YES! </p><p>Oils feel light and airy on the lips and are great for regular use, layered with lipstick, and reapplication throughout the day for a hint of color. Lip Butter Balm has a thicker consistency and is a powerful lip treatment that can be worn both during the day or overnight as a mask. What makes Dream Lip Oil so dreamy? </p><p>Dream Lip Oil has a silky smooth, buildable formula with nine oils that glide on the lip for ultra-shine and a hint of color.<br/>Dream Lip Oil does not have flavor, although it does have a hint of sweetness from Monk Fruit.</p><p>As the names suggest, Dream Lip Oil’s formulation concentrates on the inclusion of nourishing oils that give your lips a high-definition shine and hydration.</p><p>Dream Lip Oil is your new go-to companion for daily wear, whether you need to top off your lips or just need a lightweight feel throughout the day.</p>",
        "font_size": "normal",
        "container": "small",
        "paragraph_margins": "normal",
        "heading_alignment": "left",
        "text_alignment": "left",
        "text_wrap": "normal"
